cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Agentic Wi-Fi Spatial Attribution Readiness Platform — Reproducible Reference Core and Colab Notebooks"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-02"
license: MIT
type: software
abstract: >-
  Reproducible reference implementation of the core scientific machinery of an
  Agentic Wi-Fi Spatial Attribution Readiness Platform for Critical Information
  Infrastructure: explainable Bayesian localisation fusing RSSI, FTM/RTT and
  IEEE 802.11bf WLAN sensing with robust likelihoods and a missing-modality
  mask; uncertainty quantification and HPD regions; cross-modal consistency;
  a digital twin for synthetic telemetry and adversarial scenarios; a
  ten-agent orchestrator; a TRL/CRL/IRL/Operational readiness model with
  non-compensatory gate rules; and a hash-anchored Spatial Attribution Record.
  Ships two Google Colab notebooks (autonomous and pre-computed). Uses
  synthetic data only.
authors:
  - name: "AWA reference-core contributors"
keywords:
  - "indoor localization"
  - "Wi-Fi"
  - "RSSI fingerprinting"
  - "FTM/RTT"
  - "IEEE 802.11bf"
  - "Bayesian localization"
  - "digital twin"
  - "agentic AI"
  - "technology readiness level"
  - "spatial attribution"
  - "critical information infrastructure"
  - "reproducible research"
repository-code: "https://github.com/omega2417/bnt"
